+### Experimental host paging with DCP8
+
+Set `hisparse_config.enable_dcp8` to opt in on a single SM120 node with eight
+ranks using TP8, DCP8 and EP8. The Flash profile supports GLM-5.3-Flash
+NVFP4 and the upstream dynamic E4M3 block FP8 checkpoint. Both use BF16
+activations, the compact `fp8_ds_mla` cache and
+`FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM120` with FlashInfer 0.7.3 or later. Use a physical
+block size of 256 and a DCP interleave of 4. A logical page spans 2,048
+tokens. Each rank writes, stages and reads only its own 256 rows. Recurrent
+KDA state keeps its own page size so that it cannot inflate the MLA pages.
+
+Use a direct `HiSparseConnector` and a finite `host_pool_gib`. The configured
+host budget is divided among the eight ranks. vLLM provides the backing by
+default. An operator may opt in to a qualified
+`additional_config.hisparse_host_buffer_provider` that provides one rank-local
+buffer per worker. The DP-only `host_pool_allocator` remains unsupported here.
+Speculative decoding, prefix caching and extensible device allocation are
+outside this candidate's launch contract. Before registering backing the
+eight workers check their cache geometry, rank owner and provider name. CUDA
+graph capture still runs. Synthetic scheduler warmup is deferred until ordinary requests
+can use blocks allocated by the scheduler.
+
 ## Code boundary
 
 ```text
@@ -322,3 +344,81 @@ returns the lease after GPU synchronization, unregister and cache detachment.
 A failed unregistration leaves the allocation leased until process cleanup.
 This interface grants backing for one DP owner. The scheduler continues owning
 all block IDs, free lists and readiness.
+
+### Optional GPU group packing and indexer pages
+
+DCP1 packs hot and resident MLA groups into the existing GPU stride by
+default. DCP8 retains its ungrouped default. These fields tune the layout
+without enabling DCP or speculative decoding:
+
+- `attention_config.hisparse_config.pack_hot_groups=true` packs whole,
+  equal-page MLA index units into the stride already required by regular GPU
+  groups. Source/host pages, per-layer hot allocation and kernel pages stay
+  unchanged. A larger KDA page can therefore serve several MLA layers in each
+  hot/resident group.
+- `attention_config.hisparse_config.indexer_block_size=1024` coarsens only the
+  GPU indexer's logical page, expressed in uncompressed tokens. The value must
+  be a positive power of two and a multiple of the resolved source page.
+  Source/resident/hot pages keep the backend-selected block size; compressed
+  indexer pages use the native kernel block-table/view splitting path.
+
+For TP8/DCP8 with four-token interleave and local source page256, the source
+logical span remains2048 tokens. An indexer page1024 spans8192 global tokens;
+its kernel pages remain256 tokens (64 compressed rows). It does not increase
+the physical source page to1024. On the audited GLM-5.3-Flash MTP0 layout,
+packing alone and indexer1024 keep the device stride675840B and rank-local
+host stride1486848B. Indexer2048 increases the shared device stride, so larger
+logical pages are not automatically better.
+
+CPU typed-spec, actual cache-view/offset, native block-table expansion and
+eight-rank ownership/staging/decode metadata checks cover this combination.
+They do not establish GPU kernel correctness, model accuracy, OOM safety or
+throughput. Keep these fields off until a matched GPU qualification passes.
+DCP8 remains guarded by its original topology, dtype, host-backing and MTP0
+requirements. A host budget remains per TP replica and is divided by TP size;
+group packing does not add host memory.
+
+
+## Experimental full GLM-5.3 SM120 resident DCP8
+
+The full GLM-5.3 ModelOpt mixed-precision checkpoint exposes a different
+packed MLA cache geometry from GLM-5.3-Flash. On SM120, the rank-local reader
+accepts BF16 queries with a 512-dimensional latent and 64-dimensional RoPE.
+A 656-byte KV row stores 512 bytes of FP8 latent, four inline FP32 scales,
+and 64 BF16 RoPE elements. The local result contains only the 512 latent
+value dimensions and returns base-2 log-sum-exp for the normal DCP merge.
+
+The experimental `attention_config.enable_glm53_full_dcp8` option admits this
+layout for the native resident path on SM120 with FlashInfer 0.7.3 or later.
+Select `FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM120`, `fp8_ds_mla`, block size 64, and single-node
+TP8/EP8/DCP8 with interleave 4, `ag_rs`, and Q replication off. The full model's
+built-in attention defaults normally select `a2a` and Q replication, so provide
+both explicit overrides. This profile has no speculative draft or KV connector.
+Its uncompressed indexer uses 64-token write pages.
+
+The CPU contract verifies the public sparse-kernel route with real rank-local
+index conversion, RoPE score contributions, and the CPU reference merge.
+CUDA graph capture, generation quality, and measured capacity still require
+GPU qualification.
+
+
+### Full GLM-5.3 experimental host backing
+
+The same full-model opt-in can select rank-local host backing with explicit
+`hisparse_config.enable_dcp8` and the direct `HiSparseConnector`. Each rank keeps
+physical B64, with 512 global tokens per source page. The source contains 78
+656-byte packed MLA layers. The 21 uncompressed indexer layers keep their
+original B64 groups. Flash's logical Indexer1024 option is incompatible
+with this full-model write layout.
+
+The host budget is divided across TP/DCP ranks. Native pinned backing and
+an external provider use the same rank geometry and cache lifecycle. A
+provider owns the backing and may supply a callback after synchronization and
+unregistration. Its allocation must remain valid while tensor views hold it.
+MTP, prefix caching, extensible KV and other topology or row geometries are
+outside this profile.
+
+CPU verification uses the native planner and real Gloo rank agreement, with
+native and external allocation through the same vLLM worker interfaces.
+CUDA host registration, attention arithmetic, recall and performance
+require GPU qualification.
